WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.016 --> 00:00:01.627
- Oh, my God,
- Oh hi.

00:00:01.627 --> 00:00:02.962
that's beautiful.

00:00:02.962 --> 00:00:05.123
- Oh come on, thank you.

00:00:05.123 --> 00:00:07.183
- I love the colors.

00:00:07.183 --> 00:00:10.050
I was like you wear your colors today.

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:11.550
- Have we draped ourselves?
- I know we've

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:12.798
draped ourselves.
- There's the part

00:00:12.798 --> 00:00:13.890
you sit down and you're like and drape.

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:14.910
- And drape.

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:16.080
So wait, you have a cool ritual though,

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:18.270
I know, about just relaxing
kind of de-stressing

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:19.290
which I think is awesome.

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:20.280
- Thank you very much.

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:21.330
It's a ritual.

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:23.520
It's better if you have
a grill or a backyard.

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:24.690
And right now I'm living in New York

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:26.280
so I haven't been able
to do it in a while.

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:29.100
But yeah, you know how life is life

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:30.870
and we all kind of get
overwhelmed sometimes.

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:32.730
And one of the things I like to do

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:35.160
is you light a candle,

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:36.690
set a timer for 12 minutes,

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:37.920
get some paper, a pen,

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:39.720
and then just write for 12 minutes.

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:41.400
And you don't even think about

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:42.233
what you're writing.
- Oh.

00:00:42.233 --> 00:00:44.070
You don't even read it back.

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:45.840
And then at 12 minutes you stop the timer

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:48.240
and then you set the thing on fire.

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:49.740
- This sounds awesome.
(audience oohs and ahs)

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:50.760
- It's really great.

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:52.590
And there's just
something really wonderful

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:53.820
about taking all the stuff

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:56.550
that was making you so kind of worked up,

00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:57.383
and off your center,

00:00:57.383 --> 00:00:59.490
and destabilize that you
could probably scream

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:00.690
- Yeah.
and watching it

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:03.180
just turn into ash and
like turn into nothing.

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:04.350
It's really powerful.

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:05.183
- I love that.

00:01:05.183 --> 00:01:06.780
I love the it turning into ashes thing,

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:08.280
that's nice.
- Yeah, it is.

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:09.113
- All right, well,

00:01:09.113 --> 00:01:10.440
we're both gonna be-
- We're complicated creatures,

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:11.640
aren't we all?
- We are.

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:12.510
By the way, Alexis,

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:14.220
that was a beautiful story about your mom.

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:15.588
Thank you for sharing that.
- I know!

00:01:15.588 --> 00:01:16.421
Thank you.

00:01:16.421 --> 00:01:18.330
- I know and she looks
so beautiful today too.

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:19.163
- I mean, yeah,
(audience applauds)

00:01:19.163 --> 00:01:20.448
what a great audience.

00:01:20.448 --> 00:01:22.140
- So we're both turning

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:24.270
40 this year.
- We are both turning 40.

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:25.170
I'm excited.
Congratulations.

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:26.272
- Congratulations as well.

00:01:26.272 --> 00:01:28.920
I know a lot of women in the
industry get weird about age.

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:29.760
I love it.

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:31.710
I feel like life gets, I don't know,

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:33.780
exponentially better every year.

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:36.630
- I get more comfortable every
year and I get more grateful.

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:40.740
And I feel like staying
grateful is getting easier.

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:41.940
And I think, I don't know,

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:44.910
I think that sometimes
a little bit of it is

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:45.743
I've always had friends-

00:01:45.743 --> 00:01:46.710
I mean, you're probably the same way

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:48.150
being in the music industry.

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:49.860
You've had the opportunity to learn

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:52.110
from so many people that came before.

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:55.298
So I've always had friends
from older generations.

00:01:55.298 --> 00:01:57.900
And so for me, aging never
seemed like a big deal

00:01:57.900 --> 00:02:00.050
because I've always
had friends those ages.

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:05.309
But I have lost, or a
few friends have shifted,

00:02:05.309 --> 00:02:08.280
and I realize that I'm
over the halfway point

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:10.140
if I go at the same point as them.

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:10.973
- Yeah.

00:02:10.973 --> 00:02:12.210
- So the way I'm holding it is like,

00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:13.920
oh yeah, you're turning 40.

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:15.990
You might be closer to the
end than the beginning.

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:17.550
Just get to the good stuff.
(audience applauds)

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:19.182
- Yeah, I love that.
Get to the good stuff

00:02:19.182 --> 00:02:20.219
'cause you don't know.

00:02:20.219 --> 00:02:21.581
And like, come on.

00:02:21.581 --> 00:02:24.510
I mean, the world is the world right now.

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:27.240
So if you have the
opportunity to choose joy

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:31.224
then I think we are obliged
to take it, frankly.

00:02:31.224 --> 00:02:32.057
(audience applauds and cheers)
- Absolutely.

00:02:32.057 --> 00:02:35.340
I love also that you said shifted

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:36.450
because I always think it's weird

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:37.620
how people are always like,

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:38.453
you know, friends,

00:02:38.453 --> 00:02:41.280
there are seasons for some
relationships in our lives.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:44.100
And I think that that's
important that that's okay.

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:45.330
So I like that you said shifted though,

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:46.360
that was really good
- Yeah,

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:47.193
how you said that.
I don't like

00:02:47.193 --> 00:02:48.026
to say that they're lost.

00:02:48.026 --> 00:02:48.859
And by the way,

00:02:48.859 --> 00:02:49.800
I don't usually talk about
this stuff personally.

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:50.850
I think I'm turning red.

00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:51.683
You're really good

00:02:51.683 --> 00:02:52.516
at what you do.
- Oh.

00:02:52.516 --> 00:02:54.693
But no, I like shifted because I don't-

00:02:54.693 --> 00:02:55.896
- It's nice.

00:02:55.896 --> 00:02:58.680
- I think it's softer and
to me it feels more honest.

00:02:58.680 --> 00:02:59.880
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:00.870
And it's cool.

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:02.850
- Because that might not
be the end of the story.

00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:03.683
We don't actually know.
- That's what I mean,

00:03:03.683 --> 00:03:04.710
they're seasons.

00:03:04.710 --> 00:03:05.820
Yeah, people do come and go.

00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:07.350
And I think that that's
something I learned-

00:03:07.350 --> 00:03:08.183
Actually, it's funny,

00:03:08.183 --> 00:03:09.900
'cause you did say 'cause
I'm from the music industry,

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:10.920
just in the industry in general,

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:12.270
I think everybody,

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:14.370
there are literally so many
different types of ages.

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:16.470
Like there's so many
generations in what we do,

00:03:16.470 --> 00:03:17.700
especially on tour.

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:18.600
So it's awesome.

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:20.070
I think you learn from all
of those different people

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:22.590
and I think that people
come and go and it's nice.

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:24.510
And you can still be
friends with those people

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:25.950
but it's just like a different season.

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:27.695
Anyway, I didn't even mean to go there.

00:03:27.695 --> 00:03:32.673
So you did that to me.
(audience and Anne applaud)

